{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-commands/src/channel.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T05:28:02.539059Z","id":"bd6918c457a10e9a852ba2b527fd7d8e4921716182db4fa3e6ba51c3cf8c8d56","body":{"detail":"Moved from crates/clax-cli/src/channel.rs:34-40, record 90e591c9.\n\nscripts/probe-harness-env.sh was run under Claude Code 2.1.294, Codex 0.162.0 (codex exec only) and Pi 0.73.1 (pi --mode rpc); Grok Build was not installed where it ran, so GROK_SESSION_ID is not in HARNESS_VARIABLES (docs/contract.md, 'Agent channels'). Codex's interactive TUI was not probed either: CODEX_CI=1 may be set by codex exec alone, CODEX_THREAD_ID is the one to rely on.","kind":"concern","ref":"git:03275e894a555fae4b08ac4bddfee28327965aed","span":{"start":{"line":34},"end":{"line":40},"content_hash":"05249554d29894545e29cedb0e03eb88ca36c1c4cd22a62ae540d40b3319cf22"},"suggested_fix":"Run scripts/probe-harness-env.sh through Grok Build's shell tool and the Codex TUI, record the result in docs/contract.md, and list exactly what it shows here.","summary":"Grok Build's shell variable is unconfirmed, so a clax command Grok's agent runs in its own shell is the owner's","tags":["revisit:grok is available to probe","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-commands/src/client.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T05:28:02.539209Z","id":"67cb3fecf0dcca064e73490106a9f73a8707fa329aba4fb81db3a7eff8ddac33","body":{"detail":"Moved from crates/clax-cli/src/client.rs:559-572, record d105382a.\n\nThe recorded reason keeps the PID and port of the rolled-back daemon at the time of failure, which clax status and doctor print later as 'why:' (UpgradeHold::to_json, line 347), after that daemon may have stopped or moved.","kind":"concern","ref":"git:03275e894a555fae4b08ac4bddfee28327965aed","span":{"start":{"line":559},"end":{"line":572},"content_hash":"03fa82fd4bbe9374a21e0f9d43ed94372d5cc107ab701a879aa875f4f534c863"},"summary":"A held upgrade's reason goes stale","tags":["session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-commands/src/client.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T05:28:02.539285Z","id":"b5b54c3e58d29a08aa0aac65ff71c7b7e620631afd39e7c3b5f7dc753cc040d7","body":{"detail":"Moved from crates/clax-cli/src/client.rs:572-575, record 2e23fb63.\n\nClient::owner_channel makes the native host an owner channel whatever its environment, and ensure-clax.sh exempts native-host, so pairing works through the launcher Chrome runs. An owner's agent holds the daemon token and can run `clax native-host <origin>` (or call POST /api/extension/credentials without X-Clax-Channel) to mint a credential that acts as the owner's browser, unfiltered. The channel marker is advisory for the token's holder (spec §8.5 accepts the same for an agent that drops the marker); refuse_agents() in routes::extension::mint stops only the marked path.","kind":"waiver","ref":"git:03275e894a555fae4b08ac4bddfee28327965aed","span":{"start":{"line":572},"end":{"line":575},"content_hash":"6d58a0424725ddde8b8521e63c3c94f32cf02e97dfed0c1726b6525e05890414"},"summary":"An owner's agent can still mint an extension credential by running clax native-host itself","tags":["security","spec:8.5","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-commands/src/client.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T05:28:02.539352Z","id":"61be0ae8f3d949bc1044443d1758652e181387b4a1beebda51fc9a9fc462c4e5","body":{"detail":"Moved from crates/clax-cli/src/client.rs:989-1017, record e7a3616d.\n\nSignedClient::send returns a streamed answer unread for any status but 401/429/503 (crates/clax-cli/src/remote.rs:175-178). get_bytes_with then hands a 4xx/5xx answer to Client::finish (crates/clax-cli/src/client.rs:922), whose res.json() reads the whole body. A remote daemon answering a clip request with a large error body grows the hook's fetch thread without bound until the hook's std::process::exit (at most the hook's deadline, 4 s for the prompt hook), and grows a long-lived caller of get_bytes_with without bound at all.","kind":"concern","ref":"git:03275e894a555fae4b08ac4bddfee28327965aed","span":{"start":{"line":989},"end":{"line":1017},"content_hash":"08e433e13c5bc3f7c13ed93c89160fab1c1b7c8a4932a28aa902aa78250e95f0"},"suggested_fix":"Read a non-success streamed answer through the same take(limit) reader (or remote::capped_body) before parsing its error.","summary":"get_bytes_with streams the answer (exec_with(req, true)), so a non-success answer goes to finish, which reads it with res.json() and no size cap; before this change the signed client capped every body at 128 MiB","tags":["review","remote","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-commands/src/client.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T05:28:02.539414Z","id":"e32b1f58255b3251355836c668478e1856d2547316e4432f65b467ec1fc67da1","body":{"detail":"Moved from crates/clax-cli/src/client.rs:1213-1217, record 1aeed14b.\n\nReverting this canonical(exe) (passing exe as given to upgrade_recently_failed) passes every test. The comparison in replace (line 669) is tested and covers the same case, so this one is either redundant or needs a test of its own.","kind":"concern","ref":"git:03275e894a555fae4b08ac4bddfee28327965aed","span":{"start":{"line":1213},"end":{"line":1217},"content_hash":"6afdf3f37df837abdf81d28698c03335820cc56728965adb1c91a34a7439ea95"},"suggested_fix":"Add a test where exe is a symbolic link to a recently failed upgrade's executable and connect_matching must keep the running daemon, or drop the duplicate canonicalization.","summary":"connect_matching's canonical-path comparison has no test","tags":["session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-commands/src/client.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T05:28:02.539481Z","id":"a90d2165346d51296c1efbfa7428a482f5c78c14a2e3c074ae9924925fae80fc","body":{"detail":"Moved from crates/clax-cli/src/client.rs:1818-2044, record 3cdd6ce5.\n\nThey are among the slowest Rust tests on purpose: they show a daemon that never answers is stopped before the rollback, and an old daemon that ignores shutdown is terminated after the grace.","kind":"waiver","ref":"git:03275e894a555fae4b08ac4bddfee28327965aed","span":{"start":{"line":1818},"end":{"line":2044},"content_hash":"ebab617cfff5bff0dc72a09bc3eaf94bb940c7cfaa529aa81715725036e1338d"},"summary":"These replacement tests wait out the real 7 s shutdown grace and 5 s readiness deadline","tags":["gate-speed","session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-commands/src/plugin_bin.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T05:28:02.539828Z","id":"58438b7cffedb2a0c7db25e740692f7aa13a548c44a72d1c329fc2b4a5bcf589","body":{"detail":"Moved from crates/clax-cli/src/plugin_bin.rs:19-47, record ed4233fa.\n\nversion_line allows VERSION_TIMEOUT (3 s) for --version and ignores its exit status; Pi's binaryVersion (plugins/pi/src/daemon.ts:160) also allows 3 s. The wrapper allows PROBE_SECS (5 s) and needs exit 0 (scripts/ensure-clax.sh:120, 203-210). A clax whose first run takes 3 to 5 s is run by the wrapper but called 'not clax' by doctor.","kind":"concern","ref":"git:03275e894a555fae4b08ac4bddfee28327965aed","span":{"start":{"line":21},"end":{"line":49},"content_hash":"a92facfc5633cabc0b2f2baf5f2521e6ddd17ddb395b9895ee2433d71d2c3397"},"suggested_fix":"Use the wrapper's rule: 5 s and exit 0.","summary":"clax doctor --agent's binary probe differs from the plugin wrapper's","tags":["session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-commands/src/plugin_bin.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T05:28:02.539860Z","id":"a44fd7661ea049df0dbfdab55f2a4c6488da5644194202954e3faeb8ad7a526f","body":{"detail":"Moved from crates/clax-cli/src/plugin_bin.rs:48-50, record b2485554.\n\nIt reads stdout only after the child exits, so a --version that leaves a background process holding stdout open makes read_to_string wait past VERSION_TIMEOUT; and on timeout only the direct child is killed.","kind":"concern","ref":"git:03275e894a555fae4b08ac4bddfee28327965aed","span":{"start":{"line":50},"end":{"line":52},"content_hash":"711b6eb4edbc6e7e8f665352ef5abdd6798c62b7d20e6c69870055dcd822b333"},"suggested_fix":"Read stdout on a thread bounded by the deadline, or run the child in its own process group and kill the group.","summary":"version_line can block past its timeout","tags":["session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-commands/src/plugin_bin.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T05:28:02.539890Z","id":"f5ebeeac07df36fbe3fb55bf73c2660953c002babe4a21dcb4f365831c769683","body":{"detail":"Moved from crates/clax-cli/src/plugin_bin.rs:53-56, record 081306b9.\n\nclax_version returns None for a foreign program, a file that is not executable, a timeout, and a crash, so clax doctor --agent and clax bin (lines 214, 238, 355) cannot say which. The wrapper does (CHECK_WHY in scripts/ensure-clax.sh:203-210).","kind":"concern","ref":"git:03275e894a555fae4b08ac4bddfee28327965aed","span":{"start":{"line":55},"end":{"line":58},"content_hash":"08dce240c6c913454f637583c05d78519e1a32a817bd0c06aa614401e13dc1f4"},"suggested_fix":"Return the reason with the failure and print it, as the wrapper does.","summary":"'not a usable clax binary' covers four causes","tags":["session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-commands/src/client.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T15:12:24.893264Z","id":"e3f0cbf24338e7094f7e5f08edaf7164ea100ebc9ec02e23c7836bf5c3a076c0","body":{"kind":"comment","references":"a90d2165346d51296c1efbfa7428a482f5c78c14a2e3c074ae9924925fae80fc","summary":"an_old_daemon_that_ignores_shutdown_is_terminated_promptly failed once at crates/clax-commands/src/client.rs:2052-2056 under scripts/quality_gates.sh's concurrent lanes: started.elapsed() was 18.98 s against its 15 s bound. Run alone it passed in 9.99 s.","tags":["session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-commands/src/client.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-17T16:19:13.428587Z","id":"eb2975f90855b1039fff56c04bcd67e4c9deb9de66128a880195d5b53c6ccb2c","body":{"detail":"dd34a9317 changed a_slow_start_that_reports_progress_is_waited_for_and_not_rolled_back (crates/clax-commands/src/client.rs:1881): SHORT_START's start and progress windows are 5 s each (were 3 s and 1 s), so a start reporting every 200 ms stays within them on a loaded machine, and the fake slow start backfills for 30 steps of 200 ms (6 s, was 22 steps, 4.4 s) to outlast the start window. The waiver's claim stands, and the span (now lines 1818-2046) holds one more slow test's worth of wall-clock time.","kind":"comment","references":"a90d2165346d51296c1efbfa7428a482f5c78c14a2e3c074ae9924925fae80fc","summary":"Changed since recorded: the slow-start test in this span waits longer, about 6 s instead of 4.4 s","tags":["gate-speed","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-commands/src/client.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-29T18:31:48.497106Z","id":"9f41d9621681065b50ba5875e5ee3bfe4efb643bfc81a781c3182476531d200d","body":{"detail":"Moved from crates/clax-cli/src/client.rs:1818-2044, record 3cdd6ce5.\n\nThey are among the slowest Rust tests on purpose: they show a daemon that never answers is stopped before the rollback, and an old daemon that ignores shutdown is terminated after the grace.\nRe-anchored unchanged from mailto:alex@kesling.co (session:claude-code:4661063b-b304-434f-95f6-59a30e211068)'s record.","kind":"waiver","span":{"start":{"line":1818},"end":{"line":2046},"content_hash":"0ece63a8e2bc463d74cfe4ea9010f0d503f2ddb721cd763cff4ebc4304171d9a"},"summary":"These replacement tests wait out the real 7 s shutdown grace and 5 s readiness deadline","supersedes":"a90d2165346d51296c1efbfa7428a482f5c78c14a2e3c074ae9924925fae80fc","tags":["gate-speed","session:claude-code:985c579c-9fcb-4f5b-b70f-deedb4f3ea58"]}}
